[
    {
        "content": "<p>So, I'm working on getting <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/31425\">#31425</a> over the line. <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"197836\">@Jireh Loreaux</span> suggested that the new delaborator replace canonical instances with <code>_</code> to indicate that they're canonical (which is otherwise quite difficult to infer), and have the exact instance appear when you hover over it; this is a suggestion which I think is reasonable in principle and I've already implemented the first half.</p>\n<p>However, I have absolutely no idea how to implement the second! By default, it's kind of already there, since hovering over it shows the entire explicit <code>@</code> function application, but in a messier environment or if used with something less relatively clean than <code>TopologicalSpace</code> it would probably be rather harder to track which instance is being elided. Is there a way to make it show precisely the elided instance name while hovering over precisely the placeholder <code>_</code>?</p>",
        "id": 583008103,
        "sender_full_name": "Robert Maxton",
        "timestamp": 1775041412
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.PrettyPrinter.Delaborator.annotateTermInfo#doc\">docs#Lean.PrettyPrinter.Delaborator.annotateTermInfo</a> I think?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isCanonicalInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synthInst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trySynthInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">isDefEqI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synthInst</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delabCheckingCanonical</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DelabM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getExpr</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isCanonicalInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">annotateTermInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delab</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 583030122,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1775047800
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is that different to what I suggested in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/31425#discussion_r2688384132\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/31425#discussion_r2688384132</a> ?</p>",
        "id": 583090146,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1775062608
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Eric, that link doesn't seem to resolve to anything other than the PR itself.</p>",
        "id": 583092457,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1775063269
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I found it:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">canonα?</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instDα</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withNaryArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arg₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">canonα?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isCanonicalInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getExpr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">canonα?</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">canonα?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withAnnotateTermInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delab</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">canonβ?</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instDβ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withNaryArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arg₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">canonβ?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isCanonicalInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getExpr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">canonβ?</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">canonβ?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withAnnotateTermInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delab</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fall through to normal delab if both canonical</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">canonα?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">canonβ?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failure</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">mkStx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instDα</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instDβ</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 583092756,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1775063360
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's part of this discussion: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/31425#discussion_r2545561084\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/31425#discussion_r2545561084</a> (I think the links don't work because the conversation is folded when the page is opened, and somehow GitHub isn't smart enough to unfold it and scroll there.)</p>",
        "id": 583092939,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1775063413
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Mostly, I'm allergic to repeating code :p. Splitting off a second helper is also mildly unaesthetic, but definitely better than copy-pasting.</p>\n<p>Really, both <code>delabUnary</code> and <code>delabBinary</code> should be special cases of a single <code>delabNary</code>, but I couldn't come up with something with a sufficiently convenient UX to be worth the change...</p>",
        "id": 583199515,
        "sender_full_name": "Robert Maxton",
        "timestamp": 1775115450
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Anyway, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"873547\">@Robin Arnez</span> That pretty much seems to work, I'll have a new version up shortly. Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 583426439,
        "sender_full_name": "Robert Maxton",
        "timestamp": 1775208687
    }
]